WEBVTT

00:16.370 --> 00:17.400
What is it?

00:17.400 --> 00:19.370
Hurry up and put your tail 
under the lap blanket.

00:19.370 --> 00:22.370
My tail is not a hot water bottle!

00:22.370 --> 00:24.080
With a tail as grand as that,

00:24.080 --> 00:29.470
I feel like I'm snuggling warmly in a mountain 
of furs when it's just under the blanket.

00:36.890 --> 00:38.890
That's right! I have a thank you gift for you!

00:44.230 --> 00:47.710
We were able to get by until now 
as long as you dressed as a nun,

00:47.710 --> 00:49.570
but it'll be different in the town of Kumerson.

00:49.570 --> 00:52.320
It's a town with both 
orthodox believers and pagans.

00:53.740 --> 00:55.800
This tells everyone that you're a nun,

00:55.800 --> 00:59.110
but you won't perform 
any sort of missionary activities.

00:59.110 --> 01:01.240
You have to put it somewhere 
that's easily seen.

01:02.450 --> 01:05.460
What? You really thought I got you a gift?

01:05.460 --> 01:07.370
Do not underestimate my ears!

01:08.170 --> 01:11.590
I was merely hoping for something 
that would defy my expectations!

01:13.300 --> 01:16.090
So? Are we close to this town?

01:16.090 --> 01:17.010
We're almost there.

01:17.010 --> 01:19.760
We will finally have some 
warm food, will we not?

01:20.150 --> 01:24.390
I have grown sick of eating 
cold porridge in such frigid weather.

01:24.680 --> 01:26.420
Well, just wait.

01:26.420 --> 01:28.610
Kumerson is in the middle of 
opening a huge market

01:28.610 --> 01:30.730
because their big festival is about to start.

01:31.360 --> 01:32.400
Festival?!

01:32.400 --> 01:34.260
It's called the Ladra festival.

01:34.260 --> 01:36.700
Every year, a huge number 
of people come to attend it.

01:36.700 --> 01:38.240
They have many different kinds of food.

01:38.240 --> 01:39.600
I see...

01:40.450 --> 01:41.920
However...

01:41.920 --> 01:45.040
Will your coin purse be able to handle 
the purchase of unnecessary things?

01:45.040 --> 01:49.270
I've put some money aside 
for your snacks. Don't worry.

01:50.330 --> 01:55.360
In the end, I wasn't able to buy you any 
honey-pickled peaches in Ruvinheigen.

01:55.360 --> 01:57.300
Think of it as the funds put aside for that.

01:57.630 --> 01:59.500
Is that so?

01:59.500 --> 02:00.500
However...

02:00.500 --> 02:01.140
What?

02:01.140 --> 02:05.530
Will our lodging not grow meager 
as you buy more snacks for me to eat?

02:05.530 --> 02:07.870
I plan to rent a reasonable place.

02:07.870 --> 02:11.810
You're not asking for each of 
the rooms to have a fireplace, right?

02:11.810 --> 02:14.260
I would not ask for that much.

02:14.260 --> 02:18.280
I just do not wish for my snacks 
to be used as an excuse at a later time.

02:18.280 --> 02:19.950
Excuse?

02:19.950 --> 02:21.920
How terrible would it be if we had to

02:21.920 --> 02:24.540
rent a room with a single bed 
because we lacked money?

02:25.000 --> 02:28.370
Even I occasionally wish to take 
my time and rest in peace.

02:35.940 --> 02:38.970
I can't believe someone who snores so much 
would say something like that!

02:38.970 --> 02:40.180
What did you say?!

02:40.180 --> 02:41.140
On top of that!

02:41.420 --> 02:43.010
You aren't my type!

02:44.810 --> 02:47.020
You can tell I'm not lying, right?

02:52.010 --> 02:53.360
In other words...

02:54.740 --> 02:57.740
You like it when I act thusly, do you not?

02:59.260 --> 03:03.750
You fool! The more stupid the male, 
the more they like the weak!

03:04.290 --> 03:07.750
Yet, you males do not realize 
the weakness lies in your own heads.

03:10.130 --> 03:16.010
If you wish for me to be a weak princess, 
you must be a stalwart knight!

03:16.010 --> 03:18.310
Yet look how things are in reality.

03:21.020 --> 03:24.330
Well, thinking back, there <i>was</i> 
one time you acted as a knight...

03:24.330 --> 03:24.760
Huh?

03:25.190 --> 03:26.900
Do you not remember?

03:26.900 --> 03:29.790
When we got involved in that 
troublesome mess about silver coins

03:29.790 --> 03:31.020
in those underground channels...

03:31.020 --> 03:33.600
Oh, that...

03:33.970 --> 03:37.200
Brawn is not the only strength of a knight.

03:38.250 --> 03:44.090
Truly, it was the first time 
anyone had protected me...

03:48.110 --> 03:50.560
I hope you continue treasuring me 
for the time to come...

03:55.180 --> 03:56.340
I'm sorry.

03:56.700 --> 03:58.660
I shouldn't have said you weren't my type...

04:04.040 --> 04:08.720
I love that side of you.

04:09.640 --> 04:13.230
Well, I do not mind a single bed at the inn...

04:13.700 --> 04:16.440
In exchange, I would rather have 
two plates of food instead!

04:16.840 --> 04:18.480
I got it already!

04:34.090 --> 04:41.800
Spice and Wolf

05:52.910 --> 05:56.140
So? What kind of delicious foods 
do they have in this area?

05:53.990 --> 05:57.960
<b>Episode 14
New Town and Nostalgic Feeling</b>

05:56.140 --> 05:58.000
Mainly fish.

05:58.000 --> 06:03.000
I cannot imagine what kind of foods 
can be cooked with fish...

06:03.280 --> 06:05.620
They do things like steam the fish 
with vegetables and meat

06:05.620 --> 06:08.190
or season it with herbs and grill it.

06:08.190 --> 06:11.520
The town we're going to 
has its own special method, too.

06:12.460 --> 06:15.220
You'll find out when we get to town.

06:18.050 --> 06:23.730
Then, should we purchase something nice 
from those carts and make it our supper?

06:24.430 --> 06:27.320
Their scent has been wafting 
toward me with the wind.

06:27.320 --> 06:29.530
Those carts are transporting fish.

06:38.830 --> 06:39.790
Fish?

06:39.790 --> 06:43.380
Yes, would you be willing to part with a few?

06:43.380 --> 06:45.170
My apologies.

06:45.440 --> 06:48.670
All of our fish have already been 
reserved by our buyers.

06:50.670 --> 06:53.410
Pardon me for asking, 
but are you a traveling merchant?

06:53.410 --> 06:56.180
Yes, we are traveling from Ruvinheigen.

06:56.180 --> 06:57.560
If that's the case,

06:57.560 --> 07:01.600
you can probably make a trade 
with the fishermen at the lake

07:01.600 --> 07:03.560
half a day's travel from here.

07:03.560 --> 07:06.440
They've been able to 
catch some good carp lately.

07:06.720 --> 07:09.320
Oh, no. We don't want to 
buy them as goods to sell.

07:09.320 --> 07:12.750
We wanted a few fish for our own supper.

07:12.750 --> 07:14.320
Is that so?

07:16.870 --> 07:18.760
What a business-oriented person.

07:18.760 --> 07:21.290
It looks like you're thinking of 
a new business idea...

07:21.540 --> 07:24.160
Oh! How embarrassing...

07:24.590 --> 07:27.470
If you are planning to buy 
some fish for supper,

07:27.470 --> 07:29.880
are you planning on staying in Kumerson?

07:29.880 --> 07:33.200
Yes, we want to see the
 big winter market and festival.

07:33.200 --> 07:35.280
Have you arranged your lodgings yet?

07:35.280 --> 07:36.510
No...

07:36.880 --> 07:39.160
The festival hasn't begun yet, has it?

07:39.160 --> 07:41.350
Are all the inns already sold out?

07:41.350 --> 07:45.860
Yes. It's like that a few days 
before the Ladra Festival every year.

07:46.820 --> 07:48.860
Then, I'll ask my merchant 
association for help.

07:49.120 --> 07:51.900
Oh, you belong to an association?

07:51.900 --> 07:53.570
May I ask which one?

07:53.880 --> 07:57.080
The Kumerson Trading branch 
of the Rowen Merchant Association.

07:57.080 --> 08:01.710
What an amazing coincidence! 
I am also a part of the Rowen Association!

08:01.710 --> 08:04.700
Oh! This must be divine...

08:07.210 --> 08:10.510
Oops, those words are forbidden around here.

08:11.610 --> 08:13.150
It's all right.

08:13.150 --> 08:15.880
I'm an orthodox believer from the south myself.

08:16.230 --> 08:17.720
My name is Fermi Amati.

08:18.060 --> 08:20.680
In business, I go by Amati.

08:20.680 --> 08:24.140
My name is Kraft Lawrence. I go by Lawrence.

08:27.380 --> 08:28.790
Her name is Holo.

08:28.790 --> 08:32.190
We have our reasons for traveling 
together, but we aren't married.

08:36.680 --> 08:37.910
Nice to meet you.

08:38.240 --> 08:41.240
N-Nice to meet you...

08:44.230 --> 08:45.710
Ms. Holo is...

08:45.710 --> 08:48.790
Yes, she is a traveling nun.

08:49.240 --> 08:54.420
Does that mean the hardships of travel 
could be considered trials from God?

08:55.540 --> 08:59.200
That being said, it would be difficult 
to prepare two separate rooms.

08:59.200 --> 09:03.150
However, I can probably procure a single 
room if I ask one of the inns I work with.

09:03.150 --> 09:05.300
Oh, no! That's asking too much of you...

09:05.300 --> 09:09.900
Of course, as a merchant, 
I am always thinking about business.

09:10.330 --> 09:14.150
I hope you eat plenty 
of the delicious fish at the inn.

09:15.890 --> 09:17.790
As I thought, you are good at business.

09:18.280 --> 09:20.120
If that's the case, 
may we take you up on that offer?

09:20.120 --> 09:21.670
Please leave it to me.

09:42.250 --> 09:44.060
What a nice room!

09:44.060 --> 09:45.060
I like it!

09:45.060 --> 09:47.930
Yeah, we'll have a good view of the festival.

09:47.930 --> 09:50.010
Now, we must eat first.

09:51.610 --> 09:52.520
What is that?

09:52.840 --> 09:54.940
A letter from a fellow merchant.

09:55.460 --> 09:57.780
It was waiting for me at the trading house 
we stopped by earlier.

10:02.580 --> 10:04.380
What does it say?

10:04.380 --> 10:05.290
Take a look.

10:07.950 --> 10:12.290
Important information tends to arrive 
after you no longer need it.

10:12.290 --> 10:13.640
Funny, isn't it?

10:16.840 --> 10:18.770
I cannot read.

10:18.770 --> 10:20.500
Huh? Is that so?

10:20.500 --> 10:22.980
There are too many letters to remember!

10:22.980 --> 10:26.170
And there are too many 
incomprehensible combinations!

10:26.170 --> 10:28.350
Well, it was difficult learning to read.

10:28.910 --> 10:30.900
So? What does the letter say?

10:31.170 --> 10:34.210
It's warning me about the prices of armor

10:34.210 --> 10:37.320
since the grand northern expedition 
was canceled this year.

10:37.580 --> 10:41.410
Seeing the letter or not is truly 
the difference between Heaven and Hell!

10:41.410 --> 10:42.730
You're telling me.

10:43.320 --> 10:47.450
The information in a single letter 
can truly decide your fate.

10:47.880 --> 10:52.240
Well, who cares about a letter that 
does not fill the stomach? Let us eat!

10:52.240 --> 10:53.530
Yeah, yeah.

11:14.910 --> 11:17.260
Thank you very much for the wonderful room.

11:17.890 --> 11:20.510
Y-You're welcome...

11:20.510 --> 11:23.300
Since you introduced us to this inn, Mr. Amati,

11:23.300 --> 11:25.660
I look forward to the food here.

11:25.660 --> 11:29.040
Y-Yes! I am confident about my suggestions!

11:37.180 --> 11:40.200
This is all thanks to me. 
You should be grateful.

11:40.200 --> 11:43.300
Amati would probably call this 
a scam if he saw you right now.

11:46.040 --> 11:49.730
Such fine wine. It reminds me of home.

11:49.980 --> 11:51.880
And the fish is delicious.

11:51.880 --> 11:54.600
That young boy truly has a good eye.

11:54.860 --> 11:56.600
At such a young age, too.

11:56.600 --> 11:59.190
He's already dealing with 
a large number of wares.

11:59.190 --> 12:03.950
In comparison, what is wrong with your wares?

12:04.340 --> 12:07.080
Can you not deal with more eye-catching things?

12:07.080 --> 12:10.830
Or has the mistake in Ruvinheigen 
affected your judgment?

12:11.130 --> 12:14.590
It may not be eye-catching, 
but it should turn a reasonable profit.

12:14.590 --> 12:17.500
And I don't only have things 
that are dull on the eyes.

12:19.490 --> 12:22.470
You're in my cart, after all.

12:25.910 --> 12:28.100
Well, that is all you amount to.

12:28.100 --> 12:32.140
Hey! It wouldn't hurt for you to be 
a little more considerate of me!

12:32.140 --> 12:35.310
Males are quick to get carried away 
if you are too kind to them.

12:35.730 --> 12:39.940
It would be terrible if you succeeded 
and learned to repeat such drivel.

12:40.970 --> 12:41.970
Then, next time I'll...

12:41.970 --> 12:42.840
Fool.

12:43.530 --> 12:45.950
Kindness is what matters in a male.

12:47.770 --> 12:52.190
Besides, you want to be kind to me 
when I am dispirited, do you not?

13:00.590 --> 13:03.810
It is easy to forget what 
something looks like in ten years,

13:03.810 --> 13:08.300
but the taste and scent 
of things are unforgettable...

13:08.300 --> 13:11.380
This wine is similar to the one from Yoitsu.

13:12.800 --> 13:16.220
I heard when I was traveling in the north.

13:16.220 --> 13:21.110
The town that worshiped a pagan wolf god...

13:24.090 --> 13:27.310
Have you always drank such strong alcohol?

13:27.310 --> 13:30.620
Only alcohol as strong as this is fitting 
for a noble Wise Wolf such as myself.

13:30.620 --> 13:35.620
You've drank a lot. You're going 
to be feeling it tomorrow.

13:35.620 --> 13:40.950
This amount is nothing! I am a Wise Wolf!

13:51.760 --> 13:53.670
I knew you'd have a hangover...

13:54.630 --> 13:58.520
I'll have a water jug and basin 
prepared for you. Stay in bed.

14:01.270 --> 14:03.020
I'm going out for a bit.

14:16.530 --> 14:18.880
Breo, torandia. Vori pitora.

14:18.880 --> 14:19.970
Aspairo, ghanor.

14:19.970 --> 14:20.700
Marc!

14:20.700 --> 14:22.460
Vorta, yoshudaan. Habahn?

14:25.940 --> 14:28.670
Le, spandia mirt, wanderge.

14:30.170 --> 14:31.970
Pireji, bao.

14:32.380 --> 14:34.030
Looks like I'm interrupting something.

14:34.030 --> 14:38.730
Not really. He was just preaching about 
what a blessing Pitola's mountain god is.

14:38.730 --> 14:42.060
This is what happens as soon as they 
know I understand their language.

14:42.060 --> 14:45.310
There may be more profit from a mountain god

14:45.310 --> 14:48.150
than a god that never leaves its golden shrine.

14:49.020 --> 14:50.320
No doubt about that.

14:50.320 --> 14:53.580
They say that the gods of harvest 
are usually beauties.

14:53.580 --> 14:55.950
Like your wife?

14:55.950 --> 14:58.520
You've become a smooth talker!

14:58.520 --> 15:02.570
So? Did you bring me 
a profitable proposition today?

15:02.570 --> 15:05.630
That's what you're here for, right?

15:05.630 --> 15:10.300
Yeah, I brought nails from Ruvinheigen. 
I'd like you to buy them off of me.

15:10.300 --> 15:11.450
Nails?!

15:11.450 --> 15:13.350
We're a business that deals with wheat!

15:13.690 --> 15:17.390
You should sell some nails 
alongside your wheat.

15:17.390 --> 15:19.230
They're a necessity for 
your customers from the north

15:19.230 --> 15:21.440
to protect their houses from snow.

15:21.990 --> 15:23.610
Well, that's true...

15:23.610 --> 15:25.150
Nails, huh?

15:25.510 --> 15:26.540
How many?

15:26.540 --> 15:28.850
I have one hundred and 
twenty nails three-pate long,

15:28.850 --> 15:31.740
two hundred nails four-pate long, 
and two hundred nails five-pate long.

15:31.740 --> 15:35.280
Their quality is guaranteed by 
the Ruvinheigen blacksmith association!

15:36.620 --> 15:38.890
Well, I can buy them 
for ten and a half Lumione.

15:38.890 --> 15:39.910
Too cheap.

15:40.230 --> 15:41.820
Don't you know?

15:41.820 --> 15:44.400
The great northern expedition 
was canceled this year.

15:44.400 --> 15:47.090
All the unnecessary swords 
and armor are being melted down,

15:47.090 --> 15:49.000
and the prices of nails have dropped.

15:49.000 --> 15:51.510
Even ten Lumione is considered a lot for them!

15:52.590 --> 15:55.460
Isn't that only the case farther south?

15:56.290 --> 15:58.860
What's the point of expending valuable fuel

15:58.860 --> 16:01.330
to melt down metals 
during this time of the year?

16:01.330 --> 16:04.170
I'd like to see such a stupid smithy, if it exists.

16:05.250 --> 16:06.220
Goodness...

16:06.220 --> 16:08.230
Nails really aren't my specialty.

16:08.530 --> 16:10.780
How about sixteen Lumione?

16:10.780 --> 16:13.030
Too expensive! Thirteen Lumione.

16:13.030 --> 16:13.860
Fifteen!

16:13.860 --> 16:15.700
Fourteen and two-thirds!

16:21.560 --> 16:22.620
Let's go with that.

16:23.890 --> 16:25.660
As expected of you, brother!

16:25.660 --> 16:29.150
So? Cash? Or credit?

16:29.150 --> 16:30.340
Credit is better, right?

16:30.340 --> 16:35.100
That'll be great. It's hard because everyone 
wants cash this time of the year.

16:35.100 --> 16:36.300
Hey, Lant!

16:36.750 --> 16:38.470
Yes, what do you need?

16:38.740 --> 16:40.570
I bought the goods on this cart just now.

16:40.570 --> 16:43.770
Move it over to our cart. 
I'll go sell it later.

16:43.770 --> 16:45.000
Y-Yes!

16:45.530 --> 16:46.810
You took on an apprentice?

16:46.810 --> 16:49.110
There's too much to do alone.

16:49.830 --> 16:51.570
How long you staying in town?

16:51.840 --> 16:56.070
I want to go north, so I'll be leaving before 
the snow makes it too difficult to travel.

16:56.070 --> 16:59.440
But you'll be here until the 
end of the festival, right?

16:59.440 --> 17:01.050
Come over for a drink before then.

17:01.050 --> 17:02.260
Yeah, I will.

17:02.260 --> 17:04.320
I'm sure Adele will be happy.

17:04.320 --> 17:07.950
That's right. You haven't 
met my kid yet, have you?

17:07.950 --> 17:10.170
I forgot you had a child coming.

17:10.170 --> 17:11.250
The kid's already two years old.

17:11.710 --> 17:14.720
You started owning a shop, 
grabbed an apprentice,

17:14.720 --> 17:16.270
and became a dad before I even realized it.

17:16.740 --> 17:19.260
I still remember when you were 
first starting out.

17:19.550 --> 17:22.390
We were both amateurs once.

17:22.740 --> 17:27.610
But, well, the difficulties don't stop just 
because you become a town merchant.

17:27.610 --> 17:30.980
There are times I wish I could go back 
to being a traveling merchant.

17:31.390 --> 17:36.570
Even so, it's nice to settle down to do 
business with a wife and child in tow.

17:40.110 --> 17:41.910
No, forget what I just said...

17:42.160 --> 17:44.680
Well, we both just have to work our hardest.

17:44.680 --> 17:46.370
Merchants never change, right?

17:47.660 --> 17:48.590
Right.

17:55.750 --> 17:57.050
Another!

17:57.450 --> 18:00.920
Hey, you're going to get a hangover again...

18:02.340 --> 18:03.430
I shall be fine.

18:03.690 --> 18:06.730
Fine wine never results in a hangover,
 no matter how much you drink.

18:06.990 --> 18:09.980
Yet such wine pulls at me 
with painful reluctance,

18:09.980 --> 18:12.410
especially since it reminds me so much of home.

18:12.410 --> 18:14.030
It is impossible not to drink it!

18:14.840 --> 18:17.200
I'd like to ask you something 
before you're too far gone.

18:19.060 --> 18:20.200
What is it?

18:20.200 --> 18:22.480
I want to know where
 your hometown is located.

18:23.940 --> 18:26.680
As I thought, you do not know where it is...

18:26.680 --> 18:29.300
I suspected as much.

18:29.670 --> 18:34.050
You were expecting me to grow depressed 
again if we talked of Yoitsu.

18:34.050 --> 18:36.880
Do I look that weak to you?

18:36.880 --> 18:39.180
No, not at all.

18:39.180 --> 18:42.500
Fool! That is where you should say yes!

18:42.500 --> 18:44.810
So? Where is Yoitsu?

18:46.710 --> 18:49.390
Actually, I do not remember 
exactly where it is.

18:49.940 --> 18:51.040
Hey, now.

18:51.040 --> 18:54.500
I think I will remember once we get closer...

18:54.500 --> 18:55.630
Is that not enough?

18:56.350 --> 19:00.370
For instance, do you remember 
the names of any nearby towns?

19:00.370 --> 19:02.160
That could serve as a clue.

19:04.540 --> 19:09.370
The only towns I remember are 
Yoitsu and... other than that...

19:10.310 --> 19:12.140
What was it again?

19:12.730 --> 19:13.580
Nyo...

19:13.580 --> 19:14.380
Nyo?

19:14.890 --> 19:16.880
That's right! Nyohhira!

19:16.880 --> 19:19.240
Nyohhira! I know that place.

19:19.240 --> 19:20.510
You know of it?

19:20.510 --> 19:23.310
Yeah, the town is famous for its hot springs.

19:23.310 --> 19:24.940
It's a pagan town,

19:24.940 --> 19:28.470
but even archbishops and various kings have 
secretly visited the hot springs incognito.

19:28.770 --> 19:30.220
I see.

19:30.220 --> 19:32.720
When I lived in Yoitsu,

19:32.720 --> 19:35.960
it was famous as a place that could 
help heal wounds and sicknesses.

19:38.350 --> 19:40.600
Let's say the distance 
between Pasloe and Kumerson

19:40.600 --> 19:43.050
is the distance between 
the entrance and the lamp over there.

19:44.060 --> 19:45.830
That would put Nyohhira around there.

19:46.420 --> 19:49.980
If beyond that was north, 
where do you think Yoitsu would be?

19:49.980 --> 19:52.440
Hmm, let me see...

19:53.340 --> 19:54.540
That way.

19:56.170 --> 19:57.710
Southwest, huh?

20:02.170 --> 20:05.430
It's about this far away. 
It would take two days with my legs!

20:05.430 --> 20:07.160
With your legs?

20:12.100 --> 20:15.850
That's pretty far... 
I'm sure it'll take at least a month...

20:15.850 --> 20:20.240
Now I truly feel like we are 
getting closer to Yoitsu!

20:20.240 --> 20:21.510
I cannot wait!

20:22.870 --> 20:24.530
The area is too large.

20:25.190 --> 20:29.000
And we won't be able to travel 
easily once it begins to snow...

20:29.770 --> 20:32.540
Can you go home on your own 
once we reach Nyohhira?

20:33.340 --> 20:34.870
You know the direction, right?

20:35.560 --> 20:38.820
Y-Yes, as long as we get to Nyohhira.

20:39.720 --> 20:43.300
I am sure I will remember 
how to get to Yoitsu from there.

20:45.460 --> 20:47.550
I am tired of being alone.

20:47.550 --> 20:49.560
It is cold being alone.

20:49.560 --> 20:52.510
It is lonely to be alone.

20:54.440 --> 20:57.170
Hey, don't think of things in a bad way.

20:57.170 --> 21:00.800
If you can go in two days and come back, 
I can wait for a while in Nyohhira.

21:00.800 --> 21:03.280
Yes! That is enough...

21:04.210 --> 21:06.760
You will take me to Nyohhira, correct?

21:06.760 --> 21:09.500
I'd like to explore the town a little more.

21:09.500 --> 21:12.250
Listen! I plan to help you as much as I can.

21:12.250 --> 21:13.150
My words just now...

21:13.150 --> 21:16.070
While I did say that kindness 
is what matters in males,

21:16.070 --> 21:19.860
it will be troublesome 
if you are overly concerned.

21:21.190 --> 21:22.590
Shame on me...

21:23.030 --> 21:26.510
I cannot help but measure things 
by my own standards.

21:26.510 --> 21:27.970
H-Hey...

21:27.970 --> 21:32.350
To me, humans grow old in the blink of an eye.

21:33.010 --> 21:36.690
A year is extremely valuable 
in such a short life.

21:36.690 --> 21:38.890
I tend to forget such facts.

21:39.940 --> 21:43.030
I am the one who has forgotten the obvious.

21:43.570 --> 21:46.090
After all, it is so comforting 
to be by your side.

21:48.450 --> 21:51.160
I cannot help but spoil myself...

21:51.450 --> 21:52.330
Holo...

21:54.150 --> 21:56.040
It seems that I have grown drunk!

21:56.320 --> 21:59.500
I should go to bed quickly 
lest I speak more nonsense.

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Episode 15

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Bird Feather and Mysterious Ore

23:45.860 --> 23:49.500
Next Episode: Bird Feather and Mysterious Ore
